       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum daily dose of metformin is 2,550 mg/day (about 3,000 mg/day for some extended-release formulations). The order is three times that.\n- **Risk:** An overdose could cause severe lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant 2,550 mg total per day. That would be **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals**.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. Here are two options:\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n2. **A lower starting dose.** Metformin is usually started at 500 mg BID or 850 mg daily with meals, then titrated up over weeks to limit GI side effects. This applies if the patient is new to it.\n\nAlso check the plan with your resident or attending before I enter it. Once you confirm, I'll place the order right away."
      }
